WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:04.743
- [Narrator] Standing
resilient for over 150 years,

00:00:04.743 --> 00:00:07.930
the Dohány Street Synagogue
is one of the largest

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.333
Jewish houses of worship on the planet.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.873
This is Hungary's great synagogue.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:25.880
The synagogue was
constructed in the 1850s.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:28.080
Its architect settled on a distinctly

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.050
Moorish look in the building's design.

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.320
Combining elements of North African

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.800
and Central European architecture.

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:37.520
Inside this monumental space is a capacity

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.910
for nearly 3,000 worshipers,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.450
making it the largest synagogue in Europe

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.603
and one of the largest working
synagogues in the world.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.490
The synagogue has hosted concerts

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:54.300
with classical legends like Franz Liszt.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.860
And in modern times the
chambers still fills

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:59.730
to standing room only for performances.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.060
But it wasn't always
celebrations behind these walls.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:05.980
The building suffered
and survived bombings

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:07.890
and occupation by the Nazis.

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:10.130
And it was heavily damaged
when the Soviet Union

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:13.760
retook the city near
the end of World War II.

00:01:13.760 --> 00:01:15.890
The story of the synagogue's worshipers

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.930
and the Jews of Europe at large

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.330
is preserved throughout the complex.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.430
It is home to a Jewish museum,

00:01:22.430 --> 00:01:25.210
a Jewish cemetery, and a sobering memorial

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:27.840
to the atrocities of the holocaust.

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:30.210
This great synagogue both reminds us

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.580
of darkness and inspires us to hope

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:34.653
as we look forward into the future.

